PROMETHEUS AND GRAFANA – MAIN AND WORKER NODES MONITORING
========================================================

PROJECT: Monitoring EC2 Instances Using Prometheus and Grafana

1. PROJECT OVERVIEW
-------------------

In this project, we are implementing centralized monitoring for multiple AWS EC2 instances using Prometheus and Grafana.

We will launch three EC2 instances running Amazon Linux 2023.

Monitoring Server:
- Prometheus
- Grafana
- Node Exporter
- Loki
- Promtail

Worker Node 1:
- Node Exporter

Worker Node 2:
- Node Exporter

Prometheus collects system metrics from all the instances.
Grafana visualizes the metrics through dashboards.
Loki aggregates and stores logs.
Promtail collects logs and forwards them to Loki.


2. MONITORING TOOLS
-------------------

Grafana:
Used for visualizing metrics and logs through dashboards.

Prometheus:
Used for collecting and storing time-series metrics.

Node Exporter:
An agent that collects Linux system metrics such as CPU, memory, disk and network utilization.

Loki:
Used for aggregating and storing logs.

Promtail:
An agent that collects logs and forwards them to Loki.

Logstash:
Used for processing and forwarding logs in logging pipelines.


3. EC2 INSTANCE CONFIGURATION
------------------------------

Launch three EC2 instances using Amazon Linux 2023.

Monitoring Server:
- Install Prometheus.
- Install Grafana.
- Install Node Exporter.
- Install Loki and Promtail.
- Use a larger instance type depending on workload.

Worker Node 1:
- Instance type: t3.micro
- Install Node Exporter.

Worker Node 2:
- Instance type: t3.micro
- Install Node Exporter.


4. IMPORTANT PORTS
------------------

Prometheus       = 9090
Grafana          = 3000
Node Exporter    = 9100
Loki             = 3100

Loki endpoints:
http://MONITORING-IP:3100/metrics
http://MONITORING-IP:3100/ready


5. INSTALL PROMETHEUS ON MONITORING SERVER
------------------------------------------

Create the installation script:

vi promo.sh

Run:

sh promo.sh

Download Prometheus:

wget https://github.com/prometheus/prometheus/releases/download/v2.43.0/prometheus-2.43.0.linux-amd64.tar.gz

Extract:

tar -xf prometheus-2.43.0.linux-amd64.tar.gz

Move Prometheus binaries:

sudo mv prometheus-2.43.0.linux-amd64/prometheus prometheus-2.43.0.linux-amd64/promtool /usr/local/bin/

Create directories:

sudo mkdir -p /etc/prometheus /var/lib/prometheus

Move console libraries:

sudo mv prometheus-2.43.0.linux-amd64/console_libraries /etc/prometheus/

Move console templates:

sudo mv prometheus-2.43.0.linux-amd64/consoles /etc/prometheus/

Remove extracted files:

sudo rm -rf prometheus-2.43.0.linux-amd64*


6. CONFIGURE PROMETHEUS
-----------------------

Create the configuration file:

sudo vi /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml

Configuration:

global:
  scrape_interval: 10s

scrape_configs:

  - job_name: 'prometheus_metrics'
    scrape_interval: 5s
    static_configs:
      - targets: ['localhost:9090']

  - job_name: 'node_exporter_metrics'
    scrape_interval: 5s
    static_configs:
      - targets:
          - 'localhost:9100'
          - 'worker-1:9100'
          - 'worker-2:9100'


7. CREATE PROMETHEUS USER
-------------------------

sudo useradd -rs /bin/false prometheus

Change directory ownership:

sudo chown -R prometheus:prometheus /etc/prometheus /var/lib/prometheus


8. CREATE PROMETHEUS SYSTEMD SERVICE
-------------------------------------

Create the service file:

sudo vi /etc/systemd/system/prometheus.service

Configuration:

[Unit]
Description=Prometheus
After=network.target

[Service]
User=prometheus
Group=prometheus
Type=simple
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/prometheus 
  --config.file=/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml 
  --storage.tsdb.path=/var/lib/prometheus/ 
  --web.console.templates=/etc/prometheus/consoles 
  --web.console.libraries=/etc/prometheus/console_libraries

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target


Reload systemd:

sudo systemctl daemon-reload

Enable Prometheus:

sudo systemctl enable prometheus

Start Prometheus:

sudo systemctl start prometheus

Check status:

sudo systemctl status prometheus --no-pager


9. INSTALL GRAFANA
------------------

Download Grafana GPG key:

wget -q -O gpg.key https://rpm.grafana.com/gpg.key

Import the key:

sudo rpm --import gpg.key

Create Grafana repository:

sudo vi /etc/yum.repos.d/grafana.repo

Configuration:

[grafana]
name=grafana
baseurl=https://rpm.grafana.com
repo_gpgcheck=1
enabled=1
gpgcheck=1
gpgkey=https://rpm.grafana.com/gpg.key
sslverify=1
sslcacert=/etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt

Install Grafana:

sudo yum install grafana -y

Start Grafana:

sudo systemctl start grafana-server.service

Enable Grafana:

sudo systemctl enable grafana-server.service

Check status:

sudo systemctl status grafana-server.service


