19. LOG MONITORING USING LOKI AND PROMTAIL
-------------------------------------------

Objective:

We will configure Loki and Promtail using Docker to collect and monitor server logs.

Install Docker:

sudo yum install -y docker

Start Docker:

sudo systemctl start docker

Enable Docker:

sudo systemctl enable docker

Check Docker:

sudo systemctl status docker


20. CREATE CONFIGURATION DIRECTORY
-----------------------------------

Create directory:

mkdir -p grafana_configs

Navigate:

cd grafana_configs


21. DOWNLOAD LOKI CONFIGURATION
--------------------------------

Download Loki configuration:

sudo wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/loki/v2.8.0/cmd/loki/loki-local-config.yaml -O loki-config.yaml


22. DOWNLOAD PROMTAIL CONFIGURATION
------------------------------------

Download Promtail configuration:

sudo wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/loki/v2.8.0/clients/cmd/promtail/promtail-docker-config.yaml -O promtail-config.yaml


23. RUN LOKI USING DOCKER
--------------------------

Run Loki:

sudo docker run -d 
  --name loki 
  -v $(pwd):/mnt/config 
  -p 3100:3100 
  grafana/loki:2.8.0 
  --config.file=/mnt/config/loki-config.yaml

Check running containers:

sudo docker ps

Check Loki readiness:

http://MONITORING-SERVER-IP:3100/ready

Check Loki metrics:

http://MONITORING-SERVER-IP:3100/metrics


24. RUN PROMTAIL USING DOCKER
------------------------------

Run Promtail:

sudo docker run -d 
  --name promtail 
  -v $(pwd):/mnt/config 
  -v /var/log:/var/log 
  --link loki 
  grafana/promtail:2.8.0 
  --config.file=/mnt/config/promtail-config.yaml

Check containers:

sudo docker ps

IMPORTANT:
Make sure the Promtail configuration has the correct Loki push URL and log file paths.


25. CONNECT LOKI TO GRAFANA
----------------------------

Open Grafana.

Navigate to:

Connections → Data Sources → Add Data Source.

Select Loki.

Enter URL:

http://localhost:3100

Click Save & Test.

If Loki runs in a separate container or server, use the correct reachable URL instead of localhost.


26. EXPLORE AND FILTER LOGS
----------------------------

Open Grafana.

Navigate to:

Explore → Select Loki Data Source.

Select the appropriate job label.

Example LogQL query:

{job="varlogs"}

Click Run Query.

You can now explore the logs collected by Promtail.


27. COLLECT GRAFANA LOGS USING PROMTAIL
----------------------------------------

Open Promtail configuration:

vi promtail-config.yaml

Add a scrape configuration for Grafana logs:

scrape_configs:
  - job_name: grafanalogs
    static_configs:
      - targets:
          - localhost
        labels:
          job: grafanalogs
          __path__: /var/log/grafana/*.log

IMPORTANT:
If your existing configuration already contains scrape_configs, add this job under the existing section instead of creating a duplicate.

Restart Promtail:

sudo docker restart promtail

Check:

sudo docker ps

Verify logs through Grafana Explore using Loki.


