30. CREATE CPU UTILIZATION ALERT
---------------------------------

Navigate to:

Alerting → Alert Rules → New Alert Rule.

Configure the alert:

Alert Name: High CPU Usage

Metric:

node_cpu_seconds_total

Select the required instance.

Create a query to calculate CPU utilization.

For example, use this PromQL expression:

100 * (1 - avg by (instance) (
  rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode="idle"}[5m])
))

Condition:

WHEN CPU usage is above 70%.

Evaluation:

Pending Period: 30 seconds.

Folder: cpu

Evaluation Group: cpu

Configure the alert rule to send notifications to your email contact point.

Note:
The above expression calculates CPU utilization percentage. This is more appropriate than directly checking the raw node_cpu_seconds_total counter.


31. GENERATE CPU LOAD FOR TESTING
----------------------------------

Install stress if available in your configured repositories:

sudo yum install -y stress

Run:

stress --cpu 2 --timeout 120

This generates CPU load for 120 seconds.

Open Grafana and monitor CPU utilization.

Verify whether the alert is triggered and the email notification is received.

Note:
If stress is unavailable in the configured Amazon Linux 2023 repositories, configure an appropriate supported package source or use an alternative load-testing utility.


